    "narrative": "The Austin Waves' offensive core is anchored today by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (84.88) and **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29), both of whom benefit from a prime matchup against Max Scherzer. With a projected xERA of 5.23 for Scherzer, both sluggers capitalize on favorable park conditions and high-leverage lineup slots to lead the squad in efficiency. **Kyle Tucker** (76.70) also projects as an elite play despite facing Robbie Ray; his ability to negate platoon disadvantages against left-handed pitching, combined with a significant SP skill boost, keeps him firmly in the top tier of our daily starts. **Drake Baldwin** (68.60) stands out as the highest-scoring catcher, surging due to a soft matchup against Andrew Abbott and an aggressive leadoff role that maximizes his opportunity for run production.\n\nThe decision-making process for the final lineup spots remained tight, with **Tommy White** (53.43) narrowly missing the cut behind **Jackson Merrill** (52.99). While **Tommy White** offered a decent floor, the optimizer prioritized **Jackson Merrill** for his dynamic platoon advantage against right-handed pitching, valuing that structural edge over the raw projection of the bench. We are currently monitoring several \"Lineup Pending\" designations, specifically for **Liam Hicks**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Henry Bolte**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Andy Pages**. Should any of these players move down in the batting order upon official release, their efficiency scores will suffer, particularly for **Nasim Nunez** (59.23), who is already hampered by a #9 spot that threatens his path to counting stats.\n\nStrategic risks for today center on environmental factors and specific pitcher profiles. **Liam Hicks**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Miguel Vargas**, and **Sam Antonacci** are all facing \"Wind In\" penalties that dampen their power projections at the margins. Furthermore, while **Nasim Nunez** provides necessary speed,